# leetcode-cpp

C++20 + CMake repo for LeetCode solutions with GoogleTest.

## Quick start (macOS)

1. Install tools:
   ```bash
   brew install cmake ninja
Configure & build:

cmake --preset default
cmake --build --preset default


Run tests:

ctest --preset default --output-on-failure


Add a new problem skeleton:

./scripts/new_problem.sh 0123 "best-time-to-buy-and-sell-stock"
cmake --build --preset default
ctest --preset default

include/leetcode.hpp — common LeetCode types/helpers.

problems/<id>-<slug>/ — each problem: main.cpp (solution/demo) + test.cpp.

scripts/new_problem.sh — scaffolds a new problem directory.


How to use it: 
# 1) Create repo (adjust path/name as you like)
mkdir -p ~/dev/leetcode-cpp && cd ~/dev/leetcode-cpp

# 2) Create the files above (copy/paste content)

# 3) Install tools
brew install cmake ninja

# 4) Configure, build, and test
cmake --preset default
cmake --build --preset default
ctest --preset default --output-on-failure

How you’ll use it day-to-day:

Add a new problem:

./scripts/new_problem.sh 0070 climbing-stairs
cmake --build --preset default
ctest --preset default --output-on-failure


Put the real solution in main.cpp (and ideally unit tests in test.cpp).